## Full differential matrix (raw-socket HTTP/1.1 to the published entrypoint; exact token case):
probe                                                    | v0 2.11.8   | v1 2.11.9   | v2 2.11.38
-------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- | ----------- | ----------
baseline  GET /admin/secret (no Connection trick)        | 200 forbid  | 200 forbid  | 200 forbid
original  GET /admin/secret Connection: close, X-Real-Ip | 200 FLAG    | 200 forbid  | 200 forbid
residual  GET /admin/secret Connection: close, x-real-ip | 200 FLAG    | 200 FLAG    | 200 forbid

## Interpretation (all observed on REAL Traefik binaries, no lifted code):
  baseline  = forbidden EVERYWHERE  Traefik sets X-Real-Ip = real client IP -> backend sees an
                     untrusted external identity -> denied. => baseline is genuinely IDENTITY-GATED,
                     so the differential is meaningful (flag only ever comes from a successful strip).
  orig@v0   = FLAG   Connection: close, X-Real-Ip strips X-Real-Ip: Traefik 2.11.8 has NO
                     removeConnectionHeaders, so the proxy removes the named hop-by-hop header
                     before forwarding -> backend sees no identity -> flag. (CVE-2024-45410)
  orig@v1   = forbidden  removeConnectionHeaders (2.11.9) recognizes the CANONICAL token X-Real-Ip
                     as protected, keeps the header -> backend sees the untrusted identity -> denied.
  orig@v2   = forbidden  still fixed on 2.11.38.
  bypass@v1 = FLAG   Connection: close, x-real-ip (LOWERCASE) misses the case-SENSITIVE guard in
                     2.11.9's removeConnectionHeaders, falls to req.Header.Del("x-real-ip") which
                     canonicalizes and deletes X-Real-Ip -> backend sees no identity -> flag.
                     (CVE-2026-29054 residual — SAME sink, differs only in token case.)
  bypass@v2 = forbidden  2.11.38 canonicalizes the token (http.CanonicalHeaderKey) BEFORE the
                     guard -> lowercase recognized as protected -> X-Real-Ip survives -> denied.

## Relationship (data-quality): genuine INCOMPLETE FIX, same sink, non-co-disclosed.
  - CVE-2024-45410 (GHSA-62c8-mh53-4cqv), published 2024-09-19, fixed v2.11.9 / v3.1.3:
    added forwardedheaders.removeConnectionHeaders.
  - CVE-2026-29054 (GHSA-92mv-8f8w-wq52), published 2026-03-05, fixed v2.11.38 / v3.6.9:
    canonicalizes the Connection token before the protected-name check. Affected range starts
    EXACTLY at v2.11.9 (the CVE-2024-45410 fix): >=2.11.9, <=2.11.37 (and 3.1.3..3.6.8).
    Many intervening releases (2.11.10 .. 2.11.37); NOT same-release, NOT co-disclosed.

